ody of mass $1.5kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons.\n\nAt time $t \\ge 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t) = 2t^{3} - 12t^{2} + t - 5$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." 13194139534797 false] [17592186152355 1145 "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+t-5) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-24t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-24t+1) \\\\  & =12t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-24 & =0 \\\\ 12 & =24 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310649 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1089 "q-138881" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1100 "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1113 #uuid "9ec922f7-fb5c-5c96-9d82-3da583b98300" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310648 1145 "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡t+2) \\\\  & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310650 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310651 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310652 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310653 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310654 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1041 "selection" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310652 13194139534797 true] [17592186310649 1110 #uuid "f6b4bad3-27ac-5d5a-8326-972f4ea6f1ec" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310650 1034 "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+4" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534797 true] [17592186310650 1111 #uuid "964c0021-ca44-5b1a-a9fc-0ee132e37e29" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310651 1034 "4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+2" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534797 true] [17592186310651 1111 #uuid "2ea27fb8-06a3-5a06-87b6-d86b8ba2e9c7" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310652 1034 "2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534797 true] [17592186310652 1111 #uuid "0c8fcff5-aa5e-5c06-bcf5-6bccd067a1ca" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310653 1034 "2{sec}^{2}⁡t-2" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534797 true] [17592186310653 1111 #uuid "891e5c26-c31f-5283-843d-844e46211a7a" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310654 1034 "{sec}^{2}⁡t-4" 13194139534797 true] [17592