) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310716 13194139534797 true] [17592186310715 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534797 true] [17592186310715 1041 "field-1" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310715 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310716 13194139534797 true] [17592186310715 1110 #uuid "f5b299de-f350-54a7-bf19-2252c4ffc75d" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310716 1034 "2\\cos(t)-t\\sin(t)" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534797 true] [17592186310716 1111 #uuid "42e48301-3781-5b1f-ac80-f45f4f63437f" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310717 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310718 13194139534797 true] [17592186310717 1089 "q-345345" 13194139534797 true] [17592186310717 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534797 true] [17592186310717 1100 "A body of mass $\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$  At time $t>0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={e}^{2t}$ meters.\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}$ seconds. Do not round the answer.\n\